    {
      "id": 479021,
      "username": "ahsantareen",
      "name": "Ahsan Tareen",
      "created_at": "2025-08-26T13:14:37.113Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/talhabutt2508\">@TalhaButt2508</a></p>\n<p>The company structure descends from COA towards Cost center to covers branches, locations or similar hierarchy.</p>\n<p>Only one COGS GL Account can record all kind of transactions having Item Group as Accounting Dimension which can be fetched automatically from item master. The Accounting dimension then will get you all accounting reporting segregated based on item groups.</p>\n<p>You can use buying and selling Cost center in item group as well.</p>\n<p>On the other hand. You can also work with item group to achieve these reporting structure.</p>\n<p>How to do it;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>map correct item group to each item</li>\n<li>define expense and income account on item group level</li>\n<li>make item group as accounting dimension</li>\n<li>then make available item group to each item table of all buying and selling doctypes and fetch it from item master.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>you are good to go then.</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/e47774/{size}.png",
      "trust_level": 2,
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "like_count": null,
      "like_action": null,
